// LAB VERSION of queries/06-bec-sequence.kql. Generated by tools/build_labs.py; do not edit.
// Synthetic data only. now() is pinned to datetime(2026-03-11T00:00:00Z).
// Title: BEC sequence: new-IP sign-in followed by mailbox and identity tampering
// Description: Single signals are noisy. This correlates per user: a successful sign-in from a
//   never-seen IP, plus inbox rule changes, OAuth consent, or security info changes, all inside
//   a short window. Three or more distinct signals anchored on a new-IP sign-in is a strong
//   account takeover lead.
// Tables: SigninLogs, OfficeActivity, AuditLogs
// MITRE: T1078.004, T1564.008, T1528, T1556.006
// False positives: A user who sets up a new device, creates a rule, and installs an add-in in
//   the same afternoon. Rare, but it happens after onboarding or a phone upgrade.
// Tuning: Tighten seq_window for alerting. Add risky sign-in signals (RiskLevelDuringSignIn)
//   if you have Entra ID P2.
// Expected lab results: 1 row. dana@lab.example with 4 signals (new-ip-signin, inbox-rule,
//   oauth-consent, security-info-change) spanning ~43 minutes. ravi@lab.example has 3 benign
//   signals but no new-IP sign-in, so he is not returned.

